    skos:editorialNote "Curated classification (group=grp_gums_resins_naval_stores): Named gum-resin under an archaic spelling (olibanum; 'Benjamin' = benzoin, Simmonds 1892 s.v. BENJAMIN; 'camphire' = camphor) left in the residual bin. Layer-1 observations: 2 rows, 1800–1800. Series: KEW_CUST 5 ×2. Units: Lbs. (Pounds) ×2. Top routes: World → United Kingdom ×1; East Indies and China → United Kingdom ×1."@en ;
